Modification, per Apache-2.0 section 4(b)
-----------------------------------------

One line changed in each of the fourteen SKILL.md files. Upstream writes

    license: Complete terms in LICENSE.txt

which names neither the licence nor its holder, and so reads as MIT to
anyone who does not open the file it points at. In this repository the
value reads

    license: Apache-2.0. Copyright Anthropic, PBC. Complete terms in LICENSE.txt

and skill-creator, which upstream ships with no license field at all,
gained that same line.

claude-api needed a second change, in its description rather than its body.
The Agent Skills format caps a description at 1024 characters and upstream's
runs to 1068, so no loader here will read the skill as shipped. Three
redundant spans came out and nothing else: the parenthesis listing model
names no longer repeats the "Claude, Anthropic" of the clause above it,
"don't skip because it \"looks like a one-liner\"" reads "don't skip a
one-liner", and "run this grep FIRST" reads "run it FIRST". Every trigger
and skip token survives; the description is now 1018 characters.

Nothing else was touched. The remaining 214 files, every LICENSE.txt among
them, are byte-for-byte identical to upstream.


