What was left upstream
----------------------

Five of the nineteen skills in that repository are absent here on purpose,
and adding them would be a licence violation rather than an oversight.

docx, pdf, pptx and xlsx are source-available, not open source. Their
LICENSE.txt forbids, in terms, retaining copies outside Anthropic's
services, reproducing them, creating derivative works, and distributing
them to third parties. Every one of those is what merging them would do.

doc-coauthoring carries no LICENSE.txt, and the repository has no root
licence to fall back on, so no grant covers it. Its absence is a question
for Anthropic, not a judgement that it is proprietary; if upstream adds a
licence it can be merged like any other.
